  "body": "## Problem\nWhen a bot had a persisted SESSION_BLOCKED cooldown, clicking \"Wyświetl sesję\" opened headed Chromium but scheduled work still respected the multi-hour cooldown. The window could therefore look idle even though the user explicitly opened it to solve CAPTCHA.\n\n## Fix\n- when LIVE preview starts for a bot with persisted SESSION_BLOCKED, wake its due scheduler work immediately\n- bypass the persisted cooldown exactly once for that exclusive visible recovery attempt\n- keep generic workers excluded while LIVE owns the account session\n- normal job logic then surfaces/waits for CAPTCHA in the visible Chromium\n- successful authenticated work clears the block through the existing runtime/session-success path\n- if Vinted is still blocked, the bot returns to the normal exponential cooldown instead of retry-looping\n- idle manual CAPTCHA recovery still saves validated storage state and immediately releases the cooldown\n- runtime UI now explains that blocked LIVE mode is manual recovery and resumes automatically after CAPTCHA\n\n## Safety\nThe button itself does not mark the session recovered. Recovery still requires positive authenticated evidence or a successful normal job. Existing session validation/last-known-good safeguards remain unchanged.",
